# tally 2.2.1, E §11 REQ-CLOCK: "a cut an ask's literal states after `on` (`as known`, `with known`; a literal in `( )`
# too), in an ask load left standing" refuses the request, the run's one result, exit 1.
# 233.4: a reality with a scenario file. tally 2.2 answered qc alone RUN-DOMAIN, exit 0 (T's held
# fixes/scenario-files-clock).
=== options exit=1
=== b.tally
model bob
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "b card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input pay: money PLN

def twice: money PLN = pay + pay at reader

ask q: twice law 2026-03-01

ask qc: twice law 2026-03-01 as known 2026-06-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 3 000.00 PLN "the card"
=== sb.tally
scenario sb over bob
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version lower
  cite card
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-02
  replace pay = 2 000.00 PLN "a cut"

ask q_sb: twice in sb law 2026-03-01
=== expect q qc
refused: REQ-CLOCK as known 2026-06-01 is after the model's on 2026-03-01
